// Canonical CTK test: child_start_wait
// A workflow started as a child run of its own: the parent goes on at once, waits, and reads the outcome as a value.
// A runtime keeps the child's run apart from the parent's (its own journal, found again by a deterministic id) and
// reports status "completed" only for a child that ended with a result. The task Lookup is code supplied by the runtime.

workflow Child(topic) {
    run Lookup(topic = topic) -> found
    return found
}

workflow main() {
    start Child(topic = "peru") budget { tokens: 1000 } -> work
    wait work timeout 1m -> findings
    alt (work is ok) {
        note "completed"
    } else {
        halt "the child did not complete"
    }
}
